{"obs_mpwwq39k_256d67cacb7c":{"observation":{"concepts":["community features","feature planning","gamification","user engagement"],"confidence":1,"facts":["User proposed adding a modern football-themed forum","Forum intended to serve as a hub for community discussion","User suggested integrating existing leaderboards into the forum interface"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpwwq39k_256d67cacb7c","importance":6,"narrative":"The user initiated a plan to build a modern forum for football discussions. We are considering the architectural integration of current leaderboard metrics into this new community feature to drive engagement.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Strategic discussion on expanding project functionality","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:11.120Z","title":"Planning football forum feature with leaderboard integration","type":"decision"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqaoo_0d1221010ffd":{"observation":{"concepts":["Astro 5","Drizzle ORM","Server-side rendering","Tailwind CSS 4"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Project name: scoru","Tech stack: Astro 5, React 19, Tailwind CSS 4, Drizzle ORM, Node.js adapter","Project uses custom scripts for AI prediction, maintenance, and database management","Deployment mode set to 'standalone' via @astrojs/node"],"files":["package.json","astro.config.mjs"],"id":"obs_mpwwqaoo_0d1221010ffd","importance":3,"narrative":"The project configuration was reviewed to understand the current build environment and available utility scripts. This context establishes that the project is a server-side rendered Astro application with integrated Drizzle ORM and specific AI-driven automation tasks.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Read package.json and astro.config.mjs","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:20.736Z","title":"Project Configuration Inspection","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqb0v_7d3eb19664d0":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","SQL migration","Project structure","Database schema"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Schema directory contains 10 files including auth.ts, predictions.ts, and sports.ts.","Migrations are versioned up to 0010_system_logs.sql.","Project uses a modular architecture in src/ with distinct db, components, and api layers."],"files":["src/db/schema/","src/db/migrations/"],"id":"obs_mpwwqb0v_7d3eb19664d0","importance":4,"narrative":"The environment was explored to identify the database layer structure and codebase organization. This mapping confirms the project utilizes a SQL-based migration system and modularized schema files, facilitating targeted updates to the data layer.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Enumerated db/schema, migrations, and source directory hierarchy","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:21.170Z","title":"Mapped Database Schema and Project Structure","type":"discovery"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqj25_8d6863633a96":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","PostgreSQL schema","Dual economy model","KYC compliance"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Schema contains authUsers table with dual-economy tracking: crystals (virtual) and coins (real money).","authUsers includes KYC fields, performance stats, and gaming progression (level, experience).","authAiModels table links to authUsers for AI-specific model configurations.","Enums used: user_type, role, conversion_status."],"files":["src/db/schema/auth.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwwqj25_8d6863633a96","importance":5,"narrative":"The file defines the core `auth_users` table using Drizzle ORM, illustrating a complex architecture that balances gaming mechanics with real-money financial compliance. The schema distinguishes between virtual 'crystals' and fiat-backed 'coins', requiring specific tracking for both.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Examine dual-economy user table structure","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:31.586Z","title":"Read Auth Schema Definition","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqjf0_675a6313ce0f":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","Barrel file pattern","Database schema modularization"],"confidence":1,"facts":["File located at /Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/src/db/schema/index.ts","Schema aggregates modules: auth, sports, stats, predictions, imports, market, and system","The index file serves as the single entry point for Drizzle ORM or related database logic"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/src/db/schema/index.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwwqjf0_675a6313ce0f","importance":3,"narrative":"The agent read the central schema index file to understand the project's database module structure. This file acts as a barrel file, exporting all domain-specific schema definitions used throughout the application.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Exposing all domain modules in the schema index","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:32.052Z","title":"Read database schema entry point","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqji7_252c528eab36":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","PostgreSQL aggregation","Leaderboard architecture","Data normalization"],"confidence":1,"facts":["System supports three leaderboard types: Vânători de AI (crystals), Modele AI (quality), and Oracol (volume-neutral average).","Board 1 (humans) aggregates data from pred_challenges table filtered by status='completed'.","Uses Drizzle ORM with raw SQL execution for complex aggregation queries.","Relies on scoring rules defined in src/lib/scoring.ts for Boards 2 and 3.","LeaderboardRow interface defines fields for rank, points, accuracy, and delta."],"files":["src/lib/server/leaderboard.ts","src/lib/scoring.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwwqji7_252c528eab36","importance":4,"narrative":"The file implements the server-side logic for generating leaderboard rankings. It distinguishes between human-focused crystal rewards and AI/Oracle prediction scoring, using PostgreSQL queries to aggregate match data and challenge results.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"src/lib/server/leaderboard.ts","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:32.166Z","title":"Read leaderboard logic and aggregation schema","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqpm6_c6e72a399df2":{"observation":{"concepts":["authentication","session management","middleware pattern","server-side rendering"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Authentication logic is centralized in src/lib/auth.ts","Server-side utilities exist in src/lib/server/","Middleware is defined in src/middleware.ts","Multiple server-side modules (bets, duels, admin) interact with auth/session logic"],"files":["src/lib/auth.ts","src/middleware.ts","src/lib/server/"],"id":"obs_mpwwqpm6_c6e72a399df2","importance":5,"narrative":"Performed a directory exploration to identify how session and authentication state are handled across the API and server layers. Confirmed the existence of a central auth library and verified its integration across core server-side services.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Probing project structure for auth-related files","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:40.083Z","title":"Locating authentication and session infrastructure","type":"discovery"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqs8g_9efd2b99ceac":{"observation":{"concepts":["Astro middleware","Error boundary","Server-side logging"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Middleware utilizes defineMiddleware from astro:middleware","Captures uncaught errors in page rendering and API routes","Uses logError utility to report errors to admin panel","Explicitly re-throws Response objects to preserve Astro redirect/response flow"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/src/middleware.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwwqs8g_9efd2b99ceac","importance":4,"narrative":"The middleware serves as a global error boundary for the Astro application. It intercepts exceptions, logs them via the custom logError utility, and ensures control-flow responses are re-thrown correctly.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Inspection of global error handling logic","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:43.478Z","title":"Read global Astro middleware","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwqsjd_335563af1ca4":{"observation":{"concepts":["Astro framework","Authentication middleware","Session management","Drizzle ORM","RBAC (Role-Based Access Control)"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implements password hashing/verification using bcryptjs with 12 salt rounds","Handles cookie-based session management with 30-day expiration","getCurrentUser fetches and merges user profile data from authUsers table","Provides helper functions requireAuth and requireRole for route protection","Uses Astro's APIContext for request/cookie access"],"files":["src/lib/auth.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwwqsjd_335563af1ca4","importance":5,"narrative":"The file provides the core authentication layer, consolidating password handling, cookie-based session management, and role-based authorization. It maps the internal database schema (authUsers) to the UserWithProfile application type, centralizing user verification logic for the application.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"src/lib/auth.ts context analysis","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:24:43.871Z","title":"Read authentication and session management utilities","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwvv2l_25f777e1c0de":{"observation":{"concepts":["Project Scoping","MVP Strategy","Markdown parsing","Technical documentation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Decision: Start by drafting a comprehensive technical plan instead of coding immediately.","Tech choice: Markdown editor with lightweight libraries (marked + sanitizer) for the MVP.","Feature phasing: Postponed sports-specific integrations (teams/match threads) to Phase 3."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpwwvv2l_25f777e1c0de","importance":8,"narrative":"The user defined the project's foundational constraints: focus on an MVP forum structure with a Markdown-based editor for optimal performance and security. Development will commence with a technical design phase to align on database schema and implementation steps before code generation begins.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Establishing architectural direction for MVP and content editor","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:28:40.418Z","title":"Project Roadmap and Technical Stack Alignment","type":"decision"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwww480_e535b0a78d9a":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","PostgreSQL","Astro environment variables","Schema-first development"],"confidence":1,"facts":["DB client uses postgres.js and Drizzle ORM with automatic initialization.","Database connection relies on import.meta.env.DATABASE_URL.","predPredictions table uses text('id') as primary key.","Schema utilizes pgEnum for opponent types, challenge status, and economy types."],"files":["src/db/client.ts","src/db/schema/predictions.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwww480_e535b0a78d9a","importance":4,"narrative":"Inspected the database client initialization logic in src/db/client.ts and the schema definitions in src/db/schema/predictions.ts. Verified that the project uses standard text-based primary keys for Drizzle ORM tables and leverages environmental variables for Postgres connection management.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Verifying DB client initialization and primary key patterns","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:28:52.293Z","title":"Inspect Drizzle ORM configuration and prediction schema","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwww4sv_d948504a4c42":{"observation":{"concepts":["Astro APIRoute","Drizzle ORM","Server-side data fetching","CUID2"],"confidence":1,"facts":["src/pages/api/challenges/create.ts uses Drizzle ORM and defines a DuelPrediction interface.","src/pages/clasament.astro implements a multi-tab leaderboard using Promise.all for data fetching.","Prediction validation logic includes specific result types: 1, X, 2 and detailed score/goal constraints."],"files":["src/pages/api/challenges/create.ts","src/pages/clasament.astro"],"id":"obs_mpwww4sv_d948504a4c42","importance":3,"narrative":"Inspected existing API route implementation for challenge creation and the server-side data fetching pattern in the leaderboard page. These files define how user/AI interactions are recorded and how competitive ranking data is presented.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Context gathering for challenges/create and clasament.astro","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:28:53.046Z","title":"Inspect API and page structure","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwwxy20_7ccd3c1bb2e2":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM schema","Database normalization","Astro SSR","React Islands","CUID2"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Created forum-plan.md defining tables for categories, threads, posts, reactions, and reports","Enforced modular schema design using existing `auth_users` and sports system relations","Selected Astro SSR with React islands architecture for performance and SEO","Adopted cuid2 for primary keys and established denormalization strategy for counts"],"files":["forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwwxy20_7ccd3c1bb2e2","importance":8,"narrative":"I have documented the architectural blueprint for the new SCORU forum. This plan establishes the database schema for the forum module, ensuring alignment with existing user and sports data while deferring complex integrations to later phases.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Drafting the SCORU forum database schema and technical specifications","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:30:17.612Z","title":"Forum architecture planning documentation","type":"file_write"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx6b80_830a303d7a23":{"observation":{"concepts":["forum architecture","role-based access control","automated content generation","security policy","user reputation systems"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Planned implementation of moderator roles and anti-spam features.","Forum hierarchy will include leagues (Spain, Italy, etc.) as main categories with specific sub-forums for teams.","Only Liga 1 will have sub-forums; lower leagues excluded for focus.","Automated match threads will utilize AI to explain match predictions if user interaction is low.","Reputation system defined as a metric of user engagement (posts, replies, likes).","Avatar uploads restricted to trusted domains to mitigate malicious file injection (hacks)."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpwx6b80_830a303d7a23","importance":8,"narrative":"The user approved the current progress and expanded the scope to include a full-featured forum system with hierarchical leagues and moderation tools. We established a strategy for handling inactive match threads through AI-generated explanations and finalized the security policy for user avatars by restricting sources.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Defining user roles, sub-forum hierarchy, and automated content generation","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:36:47.927Z","title":"Forum Architecture and Moderation Strategy","type":"decision"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx7752_169180031652":{"observation":{"concepts":["PostgreSQL","Drizzle ORM","JSONB schema design"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Schema file located at src/db/schema/predictions.ts","aiComprehensivePredictionsTable defines core AI-related prediction data","predictionData uses jsonb storage including confidence levels"],"files":["src/db/schema/predictions.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwx7752_169180031652","importance":4,"narrative":"Performed a grep search on the predictions schema to identify the structure of AI-generated content fields. The results confirm that AI predictions are stored in a distinct table using jsonb for flexible data storage including confidence metrics.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Checking AI reasoning and confidence storage in predictions schema","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:37:29.292Z","title":"Inspect aiComprehensivePredictionsTable schema","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx78al_af8174ff7e54":{"observation":{"concepts":["database schema","data maintenance script","business logic abstraction","postgres.js"],"confidence":1,"facts":["sports_competitions table includes an 'included' boolean column for filtering.","The maintenance script uses src/lib/competition-filter.ts to determine inclusion.","Classification logic targets top-2 domestic tiers and major international leagues, excluding youth, reserve, and lower-tier events.","Classification script supports --dry mode and direct database updates via postgres.js."],"files":["src/db/schema/sports.ts","scripts/maintenance/classify-competitions.ts","src/lib/competition-filter.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwx78al_af8174ff7e54","importance":5,"narrative":"Inspected the database schema for sports competitions and the accompanying maintenance script to understand how data is filtered for the frontend. Confirmed that the filtering logic is abstracted into a shared utility function, allowing for consistent application of competition inclusion policies.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Verified sports_competitions schema and classify-competitions.ts implementation","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:37:30.790Z","title":"Investigated competition classification logic","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx7ccz_8fbdadf7fade":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","PostgreSQL schema","database modeling","data persistence"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Table ai_comprehensive_predictions maps to ai_comprehensive_predictions_table","Columns include AI user ID, match ID, and several JSON-as-text fields for predictions","Includes metadata for model, provider, prompt, and full API response","References authUsers and sportsMatches tables"],"files":["src/db/schema/predictions.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwx7ccz_8fbdadf7fade","importance":4,"narrative":"The agent inspected the schema definition for the AI predictions database table to understand the data structure used for storing model outputs. This is necessary to align application logic with the current database constraints and column requirements for AI-generated predictions.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Inspecting database structure for AI-generated prediction storage","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:37:36.060Z","title":"Read Drizzle schema for ai_comprehensive_predictions table","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx8r8f_a7c903f1eb0b":{"observation":{"concepts":["database schema design","moderation systems","audit logging","RBAC (Role Based Access Control)"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Defined forum_bans with global and category-specific scope, including expiration and unban history.","Defined forum_moderators with unique constraints per user and category.","Defined forum_mod_actions for audit logging of moderation events (ban/unban/delete/etc).","Established logic for active ban check: liftedAt IS NULL AND (expiresAt IS NULL OR expiresAt > NOW())."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwx8r8f_a7c903f1eb0b","importance":7,"narrative":"I have expanded the technical design document for the forum component to include robust moderation and audit capabilities. These additions allow for granular moderator permissions per category and maintain an immutable history of moderation actions, which is essential for community management.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Adding forum_bans, forum_moderators, and forum_mod_actions to forum-plan.md","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:38:41.987Z","title":"Expand forum schema with moderation and auditing","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx8vah_5a06d35d198c":{"observation":{"concepts":["Database Schema Design","Relational Mapping","Drizzle ORM"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Updated the forum_categories table specification in the architectural plan.","Clarified that teamId association is restricted to Liga 1 in phase 3.","Added competitionId field as a reference to sports_competitions.id."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwx8vah_5a06d35d198c","importance":5,"narrative":"The forum schema plan was updated to include a competitionId field in the forum_categories table. This change ensures that categories can be programmatically linked to specific football competitions, improving the data structure for phase 3 implementation.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Adding competitionId to forum_categories table in forum-plan.md","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:38:47.248Z","title":"Update forum_categories schema definition","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx95dg_a17dd6b48577":{"observation":{"concepts":["Data modeling","Security by design","Input validation","Allowlist"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implemented 2-level hierarchy for forum categories using parentId.","Strictly prohibited file uploads for avatars to prevent common security vulnerabilities (e.g., SVG scripts, EXIF bombs).","Defined allowed avatar sources: OAuth provider images, Gravatar hashes, and local preset files.","Implemented domain allowlisting for avatarUrl validation."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwx95dg_a17dd6b48577","importance":7,"narrative":"Updated the technical planning document for the SCORU forum to clarify category hierarchy structure and establish a secure avatar handling policy. By banning user uploads in favor of established providers and local presets, the system avoids complex security vectors associated with processing user-uploaded media.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Adding nesting logic and avatar security rules to forum-plan.md","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:39:00.314Z","title":"Update forum technical plan with categories and security policy","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx9g7h_01c9778d3a3e":{"observation":{"concepts":["RBAC (Role-Based Access Control)","Rate limiting","Spam mitigation","Audit logging","Authorization helper"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Defined `canModerate(user, categoryId)` helper requiring global role or category-specific row in `forum_moderators`.","Added moderation endpoints: `mod/ban`, `mod/unban`, and `mod/promote`.","Specified anti-spam measures: rate-limiting, post-frequency caps for new accounts, honeypot fields, and automatic `rel=\"nofollow ugc\"` for external links.","Confirmed audit logging requirements to `forum_mod_actions` for all moderation tasks."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwx9g7h_01c9778d3a3e","importance":7,"narrative":"Updated the technical plan for the forum module to detail moderation authorization and robust anti-spam protections. This transitions the logic from simple role checks to a more granular permission system and introduces specific anti-abuse mechanisms to maintain content quality.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Refined auth requirements and anti-spam strategies for forum module","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:39:14.356Z","title":"Update Forum Moderation and Anti-Spam Logic in Plan","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwx9sqi_33d445211121":{"observation":{"concepts":["Data denormalization","Reputation system","Database schema design","MVP vs Scalability"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Reputation formula defined as: postări + replies + (Σ reactions ponderate).","MVP strategy: On-the-fly calculation via query to minimize maintenance.","Scalability strategy: Denormalization to auth_users columns (forumReputation, forumPostCount) recommended for high traffic."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwx9sqi_33d445211121","importance":5,"narrative":"Updated the technical planning document to formalize the reputation calculation logic for the forum. The update distinguishes between the immediate MVP approach (on-the-fly) and the long-term scaling path (denormalized user columns).","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Refining reputation calculation strategy for forum MVP","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:39:30.590Z","title":"Update Reputation logic in forum-plan.md","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxa4vj_7895bb28d4c1":{"observation":{"concepts":["Roadmap planning","Content moderation","Automated thread generation","Lazy loading strategy"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Moved moderation functionality to Phase 1.","Implemented conditional generation for automated football-native forum threads (only for AI-predicted matches).","Added `teamForumsEnabled` flag on `sports_competitions` to control team-specific subforum generation.","Automated thread seeding mechanism defined using `ai_comprehensive_predictions` data."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwxa4vj_7895bb28d4c1","importance":5,"narrative":"The roadmap was updated to pull essential moderation features (bans, reporting, mod roles) into Phase 1 to ensure platform safety early. Phase 3's football integration logic was refined to optimize resources by avoiding blanket thread creation for all matches, opting for a lazy-loading strategy triggered by AI predictions or initial user comments.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Refining Faza 1 scope and Faza 3 automated features","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:39:46.326Z","title":"Update forum development roadmap","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxa904_2b836b658387":{"observation":{"concepts":["Moderation dashboard","Gated SSR routes","Audit logging"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Added specification for /forum/mod route to the technical roadmap.","Moderator features defined: report queue, banned users list, audit log, and ban/unban controls.","Confirmed gated access via SSR and existing role system."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwxa904_2b836b658387","importance":4,"narrative":"Updated the architectural plan to include a dedicated moderation dashboard. This document now explicitly tracks the moderator backend requirements alongside the public-facing thread and category views.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Added /forum/mod path to forum-plan.md","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:39:51.675Z","title":"Update forum plan with moderator dashboard route","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxe3ij_4e3f22e96dee":{"observation":{"concepts":["conditional automation","business logic refinement","event-driven architecture"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["User requested logic change: match threads should only be auto-created if human predictions exist.","Matches without human predictions should be excluded from thread creation triggers."],"files":["src/match_manager.py"],"id":"obs_mpwxe3ij_4e3f22e96dee","importance":6,"narrative":"The user wants to optimize the match thread automation to reduce clutter by filtering out matches that lack human-contributed predictions. This decision modifies the execution flow for the thread management system to check for prediction data before initiating new discussions.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Conditional thread creation based on human prediction availability","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:42:51.187Z","title":"Refinement of Match Thread Automation Logic","type":"decision"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxeoh2_ffb4ce9a7aa2":{"observation":{"concepts":["API synchronization","Data pipeline","Drizzle ORM","Status normalization"],"confidence":1,"facts":["live-matches API job uses `mapStatus` to normalize external feed codes (Eps) to internal status types.","Recognized live codes include 1H, 2H, HT, ET, BREAK, PENLIVE, and numeric values.","Status synchronization window is defined as [now - 6h, now + 3h].","The system uses Drizzle ORM to select matches where status is 'scheduled' or isLive is true."],"files":["src/pages/api/jobs/live-matches.ts","src/pages/api/data-pipeline/enhance-live.ts","src/lib/server/matches.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwxeoh2_ffb4ce9a7aa2","importance":4,"narrative":"Investigated the live-matches API endpoint to understand how match statuses are updated from external feeds. Identified the `mapStatus` function as the central mechanism for reconciling external event codes with internal status states, confirming it correctly handles various match phases like HT, ET, and numeric live indicators.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Reviewing API job logic for match status synchronization","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:43:18.349Z","title":"Inspect live-matches status logic","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxff0n_db6706b3f6fb":{"observation":{"concepts":["idempotency","event-driven architecture","lifecycle hooks","data gating"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Thread creation is now gated by human activity (human predictions or challenges).","Integration point is POST /api/jobs/live-matches at the scheduled-to-live transition.","Added manual trigger (\"Discută meciul\" button) for on-demand thread creation.","Enforced idempotency via forum_threads.matchId uniqueness.","Reusing existing live-match job instead of introducing new cron jobs."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwxff0n_db6706b3f6fb","importance":6,"narrative":"The forum thread creation strategy was updated to reduce noise. Instead of creating threads for every match automatically, threads will now be created only when there is user engagement or upon manual request, leveraging the existing live-match job lifecycle to avoid unnecessary cron overhead.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Update to gated creation and automatic lifecycle integration","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:43:52.749Z","title":"Refine forum thread creation logic in forum-plan.md","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxgj3s_e5716cb69d32":{"observation":{"concepts":["lazy-loading","idempotent API design","Astro Islands","content consolidation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Added requirement for match-specific thread embedding at src/pages/meciuri/[id].astro","Specified lazy creation via new API endpoint POST /api/forum/threads/ensure-for-match","Introduced MatchThread.tsx React component for unified thread rendering","Defined goal: same thread content for match page and forum index for better content consolidation"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md","src/pages/meciuri/[id].astro","src/components/react/forum/MatchThread.tsx"],"id":"obs_mpwxgj3s_e5716cb69d32","importance":7,"narrative":"Updated the architectural plan to replace dedicated \"Discuss Match\" buttons with a seamless, lazy-loaded thread integration. By utilizing a common helper function and a shared MatchThread React component, the system ensures that match discussions are unified across the platform, improving user engagement and moderation consistency.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Refining lazy thread creation and integration for match pages","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:44:44.700Z","title":"Update Forum Planning: Match Thread Embedding Strategy","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxgod5_fff5e3194fec":{"observation":{"concepts":["API design","lazy loading","sports-integration"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Added documentation for the `threads/ensure-for-match` POST endpoint.","Endpoint handles lazy thread creation for sports matches if they are missing.","Includes AI seeding functionality for new match threads.","Confirmed as part of the phase 3 development scope for match-to-thread integration."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwxgod5_fff5e3194fec","importance":4,"narrative":"I updated the `forum-plan.md` file to include the technical design for the `threads/ensure-for-match` endpoint. This endpoint is critical for the phase 3 feature that embeds a forum thread directly on a match page, ensuring that a thread exists or creating it if it doesn't.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Added threads/ensure-for-match endpoint to design doc","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:44:51.520Z","title":"Update forum API plan with match-thread lazy creation","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxivey_7a7d3b33fdcb":{"observation":{"concepts":["forum architecture","automation rules","anti-abuse policy"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Explicitly stated that human users can create threads at any time regardless of match timing.","Added anti-abuse constraints (bans, rate-limiting, locked categories) as the only restrictions for manual thread creation.","Renamed \"Thread per meci\" rule to \"Thread per meci AUTOMAT\" to clarify it applies only to the automated generation system."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/xDev/forum-plan.md"],"id":"obs_mpwxivey_7a7d3b33fdcb","importance":4,"narrative":"Updated the technical forum plan to clarify the distinction between automated match-related thread generation and manual user-initiated discussions. This ensures the implementation doesn't inadvertently restrict user freedom to start topics while maintaining the logic for automated triggers.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Differentiating manual user posts from automated match threads","timestamp":"2026-06-02T17:46:33.964Z","title":"Clarify forum automation rules in plan","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwxjl1t_58e30755bd42":{"observation":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","Astro SSR","Database schema design","Denormalization","CUID2"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses Astro SSR for pages and React islands for interactive components.","Enforces modular schema approach with tables: forum_categories, forum_threads, forum_posts, and forum_reactions.","Uses cuid2 for IDs and existing auth/role system (requireAuth/Role).","Denormalization strategy included for threadCount, postCount, and reactionCoun