vent-driven architecture","asynchronous error handling","side-effect injection"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Injected call to autoCreateMatchThread(m.id) within the status synchronization loop.","Triggered when a match transitions to \"live\" status from a non-live state.","Added .catch(() => {}) handler to prevent background thread creation errors from interrupting the main sync job."],"files":["src/pages/api/jobs/live-matches.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwyjcz8_372d06b2ba00","importance":5,"narrative":"Modified the background API job that synchronizes match status from the Livescore feed. By adding an auto-thread creation hook when a match is detected as going \"live,\" the system now supports real-time community engagement features for matches as they start.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Updated status synchronization logic in live-matches API job","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:14:56.344Z","title":"Add auto-thread creation on match go-live","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mpwyjjtd_714bcc71151c":{"observation":{"concepts":["data synchronization","source of truth pattern","API job scheduling","data reconciliation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["File path: /Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/src/pages/api/jobs/live-matches.ts","Livescore feed serves as the primary source of truth for STATUS and KICKOFF TIME","The query window is intentionally wide to handle bad scrapes and re-opening finished matches"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/src/pages/api/jobs/live-matches.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwyjjtd_714bcc71151c","importance":4,"narrative":"The code uses a wide temporal window for database lookups in the live-matches job to accommodate inconsistencies in kickoff time data. This confirms the system relies on feed-driven reconciliation rather than strict database constraints for match status updates.","sessionId":"76614519-588b-49c2-a613-dab50b89a4da","subtitle":"Inspecting source of truth logic for match status and kickoff times","timestamp":"2026-06-02